    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (76.94) stands as our clear anchor, benefiting from a prime matchup against Kumar Rocker. The combination of an elevated 4.48 xERA opposing starter and, crucially, a slow delivery to the plate that boosts his stolen base efficiency, makes **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** our most bankable asset. Close behind is **Daulton Varsho** (72.31), who thrives today against Young. **Daulton Varsho** is maximizing his ceiling thanks to an 18% boost from a favorable pitcher matchup and a high-leverage cleanup spot. Meanwhile, **Tyler Freeman** (69.03) provides excellent value at his price point; despite the moderate opposing xERA, the 14% park factor boost and the green light to run against an elite hold-time pitcher make him a highly efficient start for our pursuit of steals.\n\nStrategic lineup construction forced a difficult decision between our starters and **Drew Gilbert** (47.88), who ultimately landed on the bench. While **Drew Gilbert** carries decent upside, his projected role in the #9 spot significantly caps his scoring potential compared to the middle-of-the-order security offered by players like **Luis Arraez** (62.02) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (60.03). Both **Luis Arraez** and **Jung Hoo Lee** are bolstered today by a favorable wind-out factor and consistent placement in the order. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Will Smith** and **Geraldo Perdomo**, as their scores are currently based on pending lineups; should they shift lower in the batting order, their efficiency scores will likely regress further. We continue to monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh**, who remains sidelined on the IL, as we look to maximize our daily game cap efficiency without sacrificing our lead in the categories that define our build.",
